              Why do cats purr?
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div class="details" id="answer-purr">
            <p>
              Cats often purr when they feel relaxed, but purring can also be a
              way to self-soothe when they are stressed or uncomfortable. Look at
              the full body language and context to understand what your cat is
              communicating.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h3>
            <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-sleep">
              How much do cats sleep?
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div class="details" id="answer-sleep">
            <p>
              Most adult cats sleep around 12 to 16 hours a day, and kittens or
              senior cats may sleep even more. Short bursts of active play
              between naps are normal and help satisfy their hunting instincts.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h3>
            <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-knead">
              Why does my cat knead blankets or my lap?
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div class="details" id="answer-knead">
            <p>
              Kneading is a comforting behavior that begins when kittens nurse.
              Adult cats may knead when they feel secure, are preparing a cozy
              resting spot, or are marking familiar surfaces with scent glands in
              their paws.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h3>
            <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-water">
              Why do some cats avoid water bowls?
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div class="details" id="answer-water">
            <p>
              Cats can be sensitive to bowl placement, freshness, and odors. Try
              placing water away from food and litter, cleaning the bowl daily,
              and offering a wide dish or pet fountain if your cat prefers moving
              water.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h3>
            <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-play">
              How often should I play with my cat?
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div class="details" id="answer-play">
            <p>
              Two or three short play sessions each day are a good starting
              point. Wand toys, tossable toys, and puzzle feeders give cats
              healthy outlets for stalking, chasing, pouncing, and problem
              solving.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h3>
            <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-vet">
              When should I call a veterinarian?
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div class="details" id="answer-vet">
            <p>
              Call a veterinarian promptly for sudden behavior changes, appetite
              loss, trouble breathing, repeated vomiting, litter box changes, or
              signs of pain. Cats often hide illness, so early advice is safer
              than waiting.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <p>General cat care information only. For medical concerns, contact a veterinarian.</p>
    </footer>

    <script>
      document.querySelectorAll(".example").forEach((item) => {
        const button = item.querySelector(".question");
        const details = item.querySelector(".details");

        if (!button || !details) {
          return;
        }

        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
        details.hidden = true;

        button.addEventListener("click", () => {
          const isOpen = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
          button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isOpen));
          details.hidden = isOpen;
        });

        button.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
          if (event.key === "Escape" && button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true") {
            button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
            details.hidden = true;
          }
        });
      });
